I have reviewed Payroll against our existing Enterprise Conceptual Data Model. The current approved concepts appear to be Party, Location, Episode, Event and Laboratory Scientific Asset.

Payroll aligns naturally with Party, Location and Event. Episode may provisionally represent an employment or payroll-participation episode, although this needs semantic validation. Laboratory Scientific Asset has no identified Payroll application, so I have not forced a relationship.

The exercise also identified genuine gaps. Employment agreements, payroll periods, payroll classifications, payroll results and payslips cannot be represented accurately using only the existing concepts. I have therefore documented Agreement, Time Period, Classification, Information Asset and Document as candidate enterprise extensions—not approved concepts.

I am seeking guidance on whether we should keep these concepts within the Payroll domain model or propose them as reusable enterprise concepts through the architecture governance process.”

How to describe the models
Model	Purpose	Current status
Existing enterprise conceptual model	Organisation-wide common language	Approved baseline, subject to confirmation
Payroll alignment view	Shows how Payroll uses existing enterprise concepts	Ready for architecture review
Payroll conceptual model	Defines Payroll scope, vocabulary and major business concepts	Proposed; needs stakeholder validation
Payroll logical relationship model	Decomposes Payroll into entities and cardinalities	Initial relationship view—not yet a complete logical model
Candidate enterprise extensions	Identifies concepts the baseline cannot represent cleanly	Requires governance decision

Avoid saying, “I have completed the enterprise and logical models.” Say:

“I have produced first-pass models for validation. The enterprise alignment is based on the current baseline, the Payroll conceptual model defines business scope, and the logical relationship view is an initial decomposition. Business identifiers, attributes, rules, ownership and source mappings remain to be completed.”

